note right of DekiRuntime
  Read-only requests use focused Slice 2 modules.
  Existing write-capability requests remain on the current
  native-tool path until a separately reviewed approval
  migration can replace it without removing behavior.
end note

note bottom of Protocol
  The command protocol JSON is hidden runtime control data.
  Saved assistant text must come from say/message/final.
  <deki_action> blocks are parsed only after final visible text is selected.
end note

note bottom of CommandRegistry
  Supported Slice 2 commands are read-only and typed:
  repo code reads/search/listing, Deki library reads,
  approved chat reads, and approved public web reads.
  Exact code edits and app-data mutations wait for approval slices.
end note

note bottom of Budget
  All command results pass through budget.rs before model feedback:
  complete serialized results fit the per-command cap;
  exact feedback envelopes fit and consume the cumulative evidence cap;
  rounds, commands, trace, and wall-clock time are also bounded.
end note

note right of Status
  Prompt, status, and abort share one server-owned runtime owner
  plus Deki session id; HTTP middleware supplies the verified auth principal,
  while intentional auth-bypass requests have no remote Deki owner and fail.
  Optional auth headers cannot change a bypass request's rejected scope,
  and request JSON cannot choose an owner.
  Embedded and remote route registration are updated together,
  and cancellation wakes every waiter for only that session.
  Approve/reject remain Slice 3 unless returned as explicit not-implemented.
end note

@enduml
